<title>UK: Cable &amp; Wireless slips on stock overhang.</title>
<headline>Cable &amp; Wireless slips on stock overhang.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cable and Wireless Plc were lower on Wednesday as dealers said a large sell order executed on Tuesday was impacting the price as market-makers were left holding stock.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a bad stock position in the market,&quot; said one head of market-making at a leading brokerage.</p>
<p>&quot;A client sold 3-1/2 million shares yesterday around the 575p level,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>By 0809 GMT the shares were down 10-1/2p to 538p.</p>
<p>-- Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
